      en: "Jhenaidah is a significant urban center in southwestern Bangladesh, serving as the administrative capital of Jhenaidah District within the Khulna Division. Established as a subdivision in 1862, the city is situated along the Nabaganga River, which historically served as a major trade artery and continues to support local agriculture. Jhenaidah is widely celebrated for its fertile lands, ranking as a premier producer of bananas, jackfruit, and dates in the country. Culturally, the city is steeped in mystical traditions, being the home of the famous folk poet Pagla Kanai, whose shrine is a major local landmark. The region also boasts impressive historical sites, including the 16th-century Shailkupa Mosque from the Sultanate era. Economically, the city benefits from its strategic location as a transit point for cross-border trade with India. Today, Jhenaidah is a thriving hub of commerce and education, blending its rich cultural and religious heritage with modern agricultural industries and urban growth.",
      es: "Situada en el suroeste del país, esta tranquila ciudad destaca por sus monumentos religiosos históricos y sus extensas tierras de cultivo. Es uno de los puntos clave de Bangladés en el delta del Ganges-Brahmaputra, cerca del golfo de Bengala y los Sundarbans, permitiendo conocer la vida rural, el monzón y la cultura local. Ubicada en el sur de Asia, la región se caracteriza por el paisaje del delta y un clima de monzón tropical. Se puede llegar a través de la red de carreteras nacionales y los canales fluviales que recorren el delta.",
      pt: "Situada no sudoeste do país, esta cidade tranquila destaca-se pelos seus monumentos religiosos históricos e extensas terras de cultivo. É um dos pontos-chave do Bangladesh no delta do Ganges-Brahmaputra, perto do Golfo de Bengala e dos Sundarbans, permitindo conhecer a vida rural, o monção e a cultura local. Localizada no sul da Ásia, a região caracteriza-se pela paisagem do delta e por um clima de monção tropical. O acesso é feito pela rede rodoviária nacional e pelos canais fluviais do delta.",
